      <div type="clause" n="20.2">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:LeisWl">Leis Wl</ref> 20.2</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" corresp="#wit-hk"><pb n="506–507" ed="#liebermann"/>De relief a vavassur a sun lige seinur: deit estre quite par le cheval sun pere, tel cum il out le jur de sa mort, e par sun haume e par sun escu e par sun hauberc e par sa lance e par s’espee.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" corresp="#wit-i"><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="16" target="#LeisWl_20-2.lnote.oe.16"/><pb n="506–507" ed="#liebermann"/>De relief a<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#LeisWl_20-2.lnote.oe.8"/> vavasour a soun<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="17" target="#LeisWl_20-2.lnote.oe.17"/> lige signur<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="18" target="#LeisWl_20-2.lnote.oe.18"/>: deit<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="19" target="#LeisWl_20-2.lnote.oe.19"/> estre<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="20" target="#LeisWl_20-2.lnote.oe.20"/> quite per le chival soun<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="17" target="#LeisWl_20-2.lnote.oe.17"/> pe[dr]e<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="21" target="#LeisWl_20-2.lnote.oe.21"/>, tel qu’il aveit a jour<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="22" target="#LeisWl_20-2.lnote.oe.22"/> de sa mort, e per soun<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="17" target="#LeisWl_20-2.lnote.oe.17"/> halber[c<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="23" target="#LeisWl_20-2.lnote.oe.23"/>] e per soun<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="17" target="#LeisWl_20-2.lnote.oe.17"/> haume e per soun<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="17" target="#LeisWl_20-2.lnote.oe.17"/> escud e per sa launce e per s’espé.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" corresp="#wit-l"><pb n="506–507" ed="#liebermann"/>Releuium uauassoris, quod ad ligium dominum suum pertinet: equus patris sui, qualem die obitus habuit, et lorica, galea, scutum, lancea et gladius.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="xno" source="#robertson" n="20.2" corresp="#wit-hk"><pb n="262" ed="#robertson"/>De relief a vavassur a sun lige seinur: deit estre quite par le cheval sun pere tel cum il out le jur de sa mort, e par sun haume e par sun escu e par sun hauberc e par sa lance e par s'espee.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="506–507" ed="#liebermann"/>20, 2. An Heergeräthe beim Aftervasallen für seinen unbedingten<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="c" target="#LeisWl_20-2.lnote.de1.c"/> Herrn<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#LeisWl_20-2.lnote.de.1"/>: er soll [der Zahlungspflicht] frei sein durch seines Vaters Ross, so wie der es an seinem Todestage besass, und durch dessen Helm und durch dessen Schild und durch dessen Panzerhemd und durch dessen Lanze und durch dessen Schwert.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">20, 2. As heriot from the rear-vassal for his liege lord: he shall be free [of the obligation to pay] through his father's steed, such as he possessed it on the day of his death, and through his helmet and through his shield and through his coat of mail and through his lance and through his sword.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-hk"><pb n="263" ed="#robertson"/>The heriot of a thegn of lower rank to his liege lord shall be discharged by [delivering up] his father's horse, as it was on the day of his death, his helmet, his shield, his coat of mail, his lance and his sword.</ab>
        <note type="editorial">Added October 2026 from Robertson pp. 262–263 (text and translation); Liebermann’s text and German translation added from Gesetze I p. 506–507, October 2026 (two independent readings of the page images)</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_20-2.lnote.oe.8" n="8" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">506</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt Im</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">omitted in Im</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_20-2.lnote.oe.16" n="16" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">506</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">XXIIII. <hi rend="italic">I</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">XXIIII. <hi rend="italic">I</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_20-2.lnote.oe.17" n="17" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">506</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">son <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">son <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_20-2.lnote.oe.18" n="18" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">506</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">signeur <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">signeur <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_20-2.lnote.oe.19" n="19" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">506</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">deite <hi rend="italic">I</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">deite <hi rend="italic">I</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_20-2.lnote.oe.20" n="20" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">506</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">estres <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">estres <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_20-2.lnote.oe.21" n="21" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">506</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">pethe <hi rend="italic">Im;</hi> peipe <hi rend="italic">Io;</hi> pere <hi rend="italic">oder</hi> peire <hi rend="italic">MAT.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">pethe <hi rend="italic">Im;</hi> peipe <hi rend="italic">Io;</hi> pere <hi rend="italic">or</hi> peire <hi rend="italic">MAT.</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_20-2.lnote.oe.22" n="22" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">506</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">jaur <hi rend="italic">Im</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">jaur <hi rend="italic">Im</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_20-2.lnote.oe.23" n="23" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">506</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-bert <hi rend="italic">I</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-bert <hi rend="italic">I</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="translationFootnote" xml:id="LeisWl_20-2.lnote.de1.c" n="c" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">507</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">welchem der Vasall</hi> hominagium ligium <hi rend="italic">schwor, das, nur</hi> salva fide regis, <hi rend="italic">nicht durch Treupflicht gegen andere Herren beschränkt war</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">to whom the vassal had sworn hominagium ligium, which, with the sole reservation salva fide regis, was not restricted by any duty of fealty to other lords</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="LeisWl_20-2.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">289</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl: ligius</hi>; laut Wilhelms II. Urk. <hi rend="italic">Anselmus archiepiscopus meus ligeus homo factus est</hi>; Davis <hi rend="italic">Reg. Agnorm</hi>. n. 337</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl: ligius</hi>; according to a charter of William II, <hi rend="italic">Anselmus archiepiscopus meus ligeus homo factus est</hi>; Davis <hi rend="italic">Reg. Agnorm</hi>. n. 337</seg></note>
      </div>
